    "objetivo": "Name parts of the body and common symptoms, say what hurts with «fare male» and «avere», talk to a doctor and a pharmacist with the polite «Lei» and the formal imperative, and use «da» for how long a symptom has lasted. Avoid the English-speaker traps: a possessive with body parts, «per» for something that is still going on, and «tu» forms with a doctor.",
